  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referencing the **Georgia Department of Revenue \u2013 Motor Vehicle Division (MVD)** tag renewal website. Here's a summary of what that site offers and related information:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\ude97 Georgia MVD \u2013 Tag Renewal & Services\n**Website:** [mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx](https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx)\n\nGeorgia MVD offers online applications and information regarding **tag renewals, license plates, titles, dealer registrations, and commercial vehicles.**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd11 Key Features of the Site:\n\n1. **Online Tag Renewal**\nGeorgia residents can renew their vehicle tags online at `https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx`. If the address on your Renewal Notice is **not correct**, do not renew online. You must also present your **driver's license or Georgia ID** to renew.\n\n2. **Obtain/Retrieve a RIN (Renewal Identification Number)**\nA RIN is a **12-digit number** necessary for online renewals. To obtain it, visit the DOR website and select **\"Obtain/Retrieve a RIN,\"** then enter your plate number, name, and address.\n\n3. **License Plates**\nAfter vehicle registration, you will receive a **license plate with a decal**, which must be renewed each year.\nGeorgia offers **hundreds of specialty plate designs** to choose from, including veterans, colleges, special interest groups, and more.\n\n4. **Titles & Registration**\nIn partnership with County Tax Commissioners, the Department of Revenue\u2013Motor Vehicle Division (MVD) is charged with issuing **certificates of title, disabled persons' parking permits, certificates of registration, and license plates** to vehicles owned or leased and operated in the State of Georgia.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb Important Registration Rules:\n\n- Vehicle owners must **renew their registration every year** during the 60-day period, which ends on their birthday.\n- Georgia **liability insurance** is required to be transmitted to the state's database by your insurance company in order to register your vehicle. The vehicle must always be covered, or a lapse in coverage penalty will apply. If you cancel the insurance, you must also cancel the registration.\n- The **penalty for late registration** is 10% of the tax ($5.00 minimum) and 25% of the tag fee, beginning immediately following the due date.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcde Contact & Support:\n- The telephone number for MVD is **(855) 406-5221.**\n- Call **1-800-GEORGIA** to verify that a website is an official website of the State of Georgia.\n\n---\n\nWould you like help with a specific task, such as renewing your tag, finding your RIN, or transferring a title?",
